# tools/gen/season/vols_survey_true_witness.rish — CION VOLS Journey 13 r4, the ledger read true.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/gen/season/vols_survey_true_witness.rish
#
# The closing round of Journey 13 (Survey, VOLS). r1 made the census complete, r2
# classified it, r3 rendered it to a Bron ledger; r4 proves the ledger READS TRUE against
# an independent measure and seats it as a living pin.
#
# Two tools, one answer: vols_survey_render.sh renders the ledger; vols_survey_truth.sh
# computes the same totals a second way (grep -rl traversal, basename classification).
# vols_survey_readtrue.sh emits readtrue=agree only when the ledger's sites, handles, and
# prose_gaps each equal the independent count — free of any hardcoded number, so it stays
# true as the tree grows. The seated pin (work-in-progress/vols-survey-ledger.bron) is
# proven self-consistent: the site lines it carries equal the site count it declares.
#
# Design: active-designing/20260812-215153_vols-journey13-survey-complete-census-exploration.md
# Output convention: context/specs/20260729-215600_scan-seam-convention.md.

say "vols-true: Language EN — CION VOLS Journey 13 r4, the survey ledger read true, Journey 13 closes."
say "vols-true: Style Radiant — the map LOWE relabels against agrees with an independent count."
say "vols-true: Lens TAME — two tools one answer; the seated pin proves itself; no hardcoded number."

# Fixture read-true — the ledger agrees with the independent measure on a controlled tree.
let fx = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/vols_survey_readtrue.sh" "tools/fixtures/vols_classify_tree" "tools/fixtures/vols_classify_guardlist_ok.txt"]
say fx.out
assert fx.out contains "readtrue=agree" else "vols-true: the fixture ledger disagreed with the independent measure"
assert fx.ok else "vols-true: fixture read-true verdict and status disagree"

# Live read-true — the ledger and the independent grep -rl measure agree on the real tree.
let live = run ["sh" "-c" "sh tools/fixtures/vols_guardlist_extract.sh tools/gen/season/cion_module_labeling_witness.rish > /tmp/vols_live_guardlist.txt && sh tools/fixtures/vols_survey_readtrue.sh . /tmp/vols_live_guardlist.txt"]
say live.out
assert live.out contains "readtrue=agree" else "vols-true: the live ledger disagreed with the independent measure — the survey does not read true"
assert live.ok else "vols-true: live read-true verdict and status disagree"

# The seated pin exists, is a real cion-survey-v1 ledger, and parses.
let pin = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/vols_survey_parse.sh" "work-in-progress/vols-survey-ledger.bron"]
say pin.out
assert pin.out contains "verdict=ok" else "vols-true: the seated survey ledger did not parse"
assert pin.ok else "vols-true: the seated ledger verdict and status disagree"
assert pin.out contains "guarded_sites=0" else "vols-true: the seated ledger reports a drifted guarded file"

# The pin proves itself — the site lines it carries equal the site count it declares, no
# number hardcoded here (so a future re-seat at a new stamp keeps this witness true).
let selfcheck = run ["sh" "-c" "p=$(sh tools/fixtures/vols_survey_parse.sh work-in-progress/vols-survey-ledger.bron); s=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$p\" | sed -n 's/^sites=//p'); l=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$p\" | sed -n 's/^site_lines=//p'); if [ \"$s\" = \"$l\" ]; then echo consistent=yes; else echo consistent=no; fi"]
say selfcheck.out
assert selfcheck.out contains "consistent=yes" else "vols-true: the seated ledger's declared site count disagrees with the site lines it carries"

say "GREEN: vols-true — the survey ledger reads true against an independent measure (two tools, one answer), the seated living pin work-in-progress/vols-survey-ledger.bron proves itself self-consistent, and Journey 13 (Survey, VOLS) stands complete — the map LOWE relabels against is on metal"
